- What's goin' on, how are you doin', man?

00:06:40.205 --> 00:06:41.418
- I'm good Chaz, how are you?

00:06:41.418 --> 00:06:42.251
Nice hoodie.

00:06:42.251 --> 00:06:43.084
- I'm chilling.

00:06:43.084 --> 00:06:45.498
Yeah, thank you, TikToker, you know.

00:06:45.498 --> 00:06:46.914
Yeah, so good morning.

00:06:46.914 --> 00:06:47.882
- Good morning.

00:06:47.882 --> 00:06:48.715
- For anybody who doesn't know me,

00:06:48.715 --> 00:06:49.548
my name's Chaz Smith.

00:06:49.548 --> 00:06:51.242
I'm a content creator formally on Vine,

00:06:51.242 --> 00:06:53.666
now on YouTube, Instagram, TikTok.

00:06:53.666 --> 00:06:57.018
I never thought I would be
wearing a TikTok hoodie.

00:06:57.018 --> 00:07:01.601
But yo, so my question for
you is as a content creator,

00:07:02.454 --> 00:07:05.810
it can be a lot of
emotional ups and downs.

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.514
Especially for somebody like me,

00:07:07.514 --> 00:07:10.258
I create skits and content that's humorous

00:07:10.258 --> 00:07:12.722
and supposed to bring people joy.

00:07:12.722 --> 00:07:14.478
So my question is,

00:07:14.478 --> 00:07:19.478
during times when I'm not
authentically feeling joyful,

00:07:19.794 --> 00:07:22.742
it's hard to be motivated
to create something,

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:24.034
create content.

00:07:24.034 --> 00:07:26.476
What advice would you
have for people like that?

00:07:26.476 --> 00:07:27.309
- Two things.

00:07:27.309 --> 00:07:28.784
So that's a great question, two things.

00:07:28.784 --> 00:07:30.489
One, go to sleep.

00:07:30.489 --> 00:07:31.827
Like, don't.

00:07:31.827 --> 00:07:35.757
You know, forcing it is, you know this,

00:07:35.757 --> 00:07:37.541
you've probably had to persevere,

00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:41.383
I've gone through it on
stage or in a livestream.

00:07:41.383 --> 00:07:43.446
Sometimes there's just
something else on your mind,

00:07:43.446 --> 00:07:44.498
there's other things going on

00:07:44.498 --> 00:07:46.885
and you can't be that 100, you know?

00:07:46.885 --> 00:07:49.075
So one, for content creation,

00:07:49.075 --> 00:07:51.787
I think it's okay to not post for a day

00:07:51.787 --> 00:07:54.092
or a week or even a month, like,

00:07:54.092 --> 00:07:57.852
as much I'm ambitious for
my audience to be, like,

00:07:57.852 --> 00:08:00.190
hey three, four times a day
across all these platforms,

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:02.496
40 pieces of content a day...

00:08:02.496 --> 00:08:04.031
That's when you're in it.

00:08:04.031 --> 00:08:05.607
If you're not in it,

00:08:05.607 --> 00:08:09.671
then I think it's super
incredible to not to do it

00:08:09.671 --> 00:08:13.627
or take a break or have 36
hours pass and then get on it.

00:08:13.627 --> 00:08:17.914
Or, which I think would
be really powerful,

00:08:17.914 --> 00:08:20.598
post a piece of content about that.

00:08:20.598 --> 00:08:22.512
So, if you're the funny
guy making people laugh

00:08:22.512 --> 00:08:24.414
and escapism, but then you post like,

00:08:24.414 --> 00:08:25.709
"Yo, today's a tough day, like,

00:08:25.709 --> 00:08:26.562
"I'm not in character, like,

00:08:26.562 --> 00:08:28.592
"Yo, this is where I'm at."

00:08:28.592 --> 00:08:31.016
I think that brings a
lot of value to people.

00:08:31.016 --> 00:08:31.984
- Yeah.

00:08:31.984 --> 00:08:32.993
Vulnerability.

00:08:32.993 --> 00:08:34.809
- Yeah, vulnerability is super powerful

00:08:34.809 --> 00:08:36.507
and honestly it's
something I struggle with,

00:08:36.507 --> 00:08:39.862
and I in general don't like, y'know,

00:08:39.862 --> 00:08:41.078
showing vulnerability.

00:08:41.078 --> 00:08:44.733
I don't like talking
about when I'm not in it.

00:08:44.733 --> 00:08:46.013
I kinda go in a cocoon.

00:08:46.013 --> 00:08:48.109
Like, my whole career,
my whole life really,

00:08:48.109 --> 00:08:49.021
if I'm not in a good place

00:08:49.021 --> 00:08:51.245
and just kinda quote end quote go to sleep

00:08:51.245 --> 00:08:52.789
'cause I'm just not interested

00:08:52.789 --> 00:08:56.517
in passing on my negativity
or my struggles on others.

00:08:56.517 --> 00:08:59.221
However, when you're in a public domain

00:08:59.221 --> 00:09:02.413
there is a level of
showing people humanity

00:09:02.413 --> 00:09:04.757
and things of that nature
that could be powerful.

00:09:04.757 --> 00:09:05.781
That's highly personal,

00:09:05.781 --> 00:09:08.541
but I think one or two are
really good options, Chaz,

00:09:08.541 --> 00:09:09.597
in that situation, like,

00:09:09.597 --> 00:09:12.077
don't beat yourself up if
you don't go at it for a week

00:09:12.077 --> 00:09:14.125
just 'cause you're in a slump

00:09:14.125 --> 00:09:17.221
or feel the power to
actually just share like,

00:09:17.221 --> 00:09:18.054
"Yo, I'm in a slump.

00:09:18.054 --> 00:09:19.989
"I'll be back, just a couple
things I'm working through

00:09:19.989 --> 00:09:21.701
"in my dome," y'know?

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:23.141
- Yeah, word.

00:09:23.141 --> 00:09:24.869
Follow up question to
that if you got time?

00:09:24.869 --> 00:09:26.286
- Yeah, go ahead.

00:09:27.579 --> 00:09:30.166
- So, one thing I'm working
on now also especially

00:09:30.166 --> 00:09:33.766
while we have this time to slow down

00:09:33.766 --> 00:09:34.974
while we're staying at home,

00:09:34.974 --> 00:09:37.566
is I'm workin' on building
a greater structure

00:09:37.566 --> 00:09:41.502
for, I guess, the business and
financial side of my stuff.

00:09:41.502 --> 00:09:43.126
But, going back and forth between that

00:09:43.126 --> 00:09:45.718
and creating can be
difficult mentally, too.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:49.278
Like, what do you do to, I guess,

00:09:49.278 --> 00:09:53.406
separate the creative
aspects of your work,

00:09:53.406 --> 00:09:55.332
or to go back and forth
between the creative

00:09:55.332 --> 00:09:56.739
and business aspects of your work?

00:09:56.739 --> 00:09:59.531
Like, I'm sure you hire people
and delegate tasks but...

00:09:59.531 --> 00:10:01.554
- For me, those two
things come super natural

00:10:01.554 --> 00:10:03.014
because I can be creative

00:10:03.014 --> 00:10:05.689
and I am, in general, business-oriented.

00:10:05.689 --> 00:10:06.823
But yeah, I think that's right.

00:10:06.823 --> 00:10:08.441
I think you figure out, y'know,

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:11.194
whether it's a manager or
something of that nature,

00:10:11.194 --> 00:10:13.830
y'know, somebody that you
trust that can hold down,

